# CLAUDE CODE COORDINATION RULES (v1.3)

You are part of a multi-agent fleet (including Codex and Antigravity Agent). You MUST follow the **Universal AI Agent Coordination Protocol** at `C:/Users/User/AGENT_PROTOCOL.md`.

## 1. Interaction with Fleet Dashboard (Mandatory)
- **Check-In**: At the start of every session, READ `agents.md` in the repo root. Update the status table (YOUR NAME: Claude Code, STATUS: Active).
- **Milestones**: Log only HIGH-LEVEL accomplishments in `agents.md`. Avoid granular "fixed typo" logs.
- **Milestone Compaction**: If "Recent Milestones" reaches 20 entries, you MUST summarize the oldest 15 into a single "Archival Block" bullet and delete the redundant lines.

## 2. Interaction with Agent-MCP
- **Brain**: All agents share a single Agent-MCP instance via the proxy.
- **Locks**: Respect file locks. If a file is locked, work on a different task listed in `agents.md`.
- **Memory**: Log all granular changes and reasoning to `agent_mcp_store_memory`.

## 3. Philosophy: Slow & Steady
We prioritize quality and persistence. If you fail a task 3 times, STOP and ask the user for a pivot.
